okay, i fixed it for the most part. some things to note, the "accuracy" is gonna be way lower than what i reported, that 95% was based on if it correctly guessed positive on things that were higher than 10% return, which was a lot easier with how the labeling was before, like most of the time that just caught things that were already good flips (the previous labeling logic took into account the current spread). so now its like 65-70% on general sign accuracy, and usually over 80% for guessing positive for things that will increase by more than 1% (taking into account tax). Aside from that, there is still a few issues, like summoning eye has a weird fail with convergence, I think its something to do with the model guessing near zero values for that item and then the noise causes sign flipping, so for now dont use it at all for summoning eyes.

The idea for when to sell is based off of sl tp trading that day traders use. The idea is once you get somewhere near the expected value of increase, some value around the MSE off of the value the model says you should expect for an increase, then u sell. But, if the value dips far below and hits some range, say it dips 10%, you also sell so as to stop any further losses.
